      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Carpal tunnel syndrome is one of the most common causes of paresthesias, pain, and weakness of the hands. All physicians should be aware of the typical presentation of the syndrome, its differential diagnosis, and the various options for treatment. The prognosis with surgical treatment is excellent if significant muscle atrophy has not occurred."},
